Version: 1.0
desc: Reel Talk Tape Machine (CHOW Tape Model port) by chmaha
tags: tape saturation hysteresis wow flutter lofi analog effect
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  A physically modelled reel-to-reel tape machine. The heart of it is a magnetic hysteresis model
  of the tape itself (Drive, Saturation and Bias), solved with your choice of Runge-Kutta or
  Newton-Raphson solvers, a small neural network (STN) or the original v1 sound, and oversampled
  up to 16x. Around it sit the rest of the machine: input filters, tone, a tape-style compressor,
  playback head loss (speed, spacing, thickness, gap and azimuth, with the head bump), wow and
  flutter, degradation noise and "chew" for damaged tape, plus mid/side and stereo balance.
  Comes with the 95 factory presets.
  Needs Dependencies/ReelTalk/stn_weights.txt for the STN tape mode.
  Ported from CHOW Tape Model by Jatin Chowdhury (Chowdhury DSP)
  https://github.com/jatinchowdhury18/AnalogTapeModel (GPLv3)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/ReelTalk/stn_weights.txt

